  :adr/body "# ADR-2607258000: `manifest/west.yml` emptied twice by a registration write path

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-25
**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki
**Scope**: `com-junkawasaki/root`

## What happened

`manifest/west.yml` reached `main` as a **0-byte file twice in one day**, both
times from the same entry-registration path:

| commit | subject | size after |
|---|---|---|
| `ad193ef4` | chore(manifest): add abi west entry | **0** |
| `0bd2b5e18` | fix(manifest): restore west.yml — ad193ef4 emptied it entirely | 725,746 |
| `7803359c` | chore(manifest): advance abi pin | **0** |
| `e23fdf309` | manifest: restore west.yml (emptied AGAIN by 7803359) + advance pins | 725,746 |

With an empty manifest, `west update` resolves **no projects at all**. The
second-order damage is quieter: a concurrent single-entry pin edit (murakumo
`5a7a55fe → 4551bcc7`) was applied by search-and-replace against the emptied
file, matched nothing, exited 0, and merged as a no-op. It was caught only by
reading the manifest back from `main` afterwards, and re-applied.

## Why the existing guards did not catch it

`scripts/verify-west-pins.cljs` and the PreToolUse guard check that each pin is
a commit reachable from its upstream default branch. **An empty file satisfies
that trivially** — it declares no pins, so there is nothing to fail. Pin
reachability and structural integrity are different properties, and only the
first is enforced.

## Repair

Restore the last good blob and re-apply only the single-entry edits made in the
interval — never regenerate wholesale (the standing manifest rule already says
this, because regeneration pins from local working HEADs and can silently roll
pins back). The restored content here is byte-identical to the pre-break state
(725,746 bytes, 3,725 projects, sha256 `77ea9ecf…`).

Two sessions prepared a restore at the same time; the one that lost the race
(HTTP 409) re-read the tip, dropped its redundant restore, and landed only its
own one-line pin edit. No force-push, per the standing rule.

## What is still missing

**`kotoba-lang/abi` has no entry in the manifest.** Its registration never
landed — both restore points predate it, and an empty-file diff carries no
information about the intended pin, so it cannot be reconstructed by a third
party. Whoever owns that work should fix the write path that produced two empty
files, then re-register with `gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry abi`.

## Follow-up

Add a structural floor for `manifest/west.yml` alongside the pin verifier: fail
a write whose result is zero bytes, or whose project count drops by more than a
small delta from the parent commit. That is the check that would have stopped
both incidents at the source instead of after the fact."}]
